Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.00,0:00:34.14,Kick,,0,0,0,,WORLD · EXPLAINED
Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.00,0:00:34.14,Title,,0,0,0,,THE COURT\NSAYS GENOCIDE
Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.00,0:00:34.14,Foot,,0,0,0,,Source: Radio Free Asia · Jerusalem Post · The Hill\NFull video on the channel
Dialogue: 1,0:00:00.15,0:00:02.40,Big,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1640)\fad(120,150)}9 – 6
Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.00,0:00:04.97,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}A world court just ruled a country committed genocide, by nine votes to six.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:05.42,0:00:12.70,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}The judges said soldiers, police and border guards killed around ten thousand Ro hin ja civilians in two thousand seventeen.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:13.15,0:00:15.58,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}Hundreds of thousands fled to Bangladesh.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:15.58,0:00:19.38,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}About one point two million Ro hin ja still live in camps there.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:19.83,0:00:24.00,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}The case was brought in twenty nineteen by a small country, The Gambia.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:24.00,0:00:28.40,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}Myanmar says its operations were a response to attacks by a militant group.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:28.85,0:00:29.71,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}Why it matters:
Dialogue: 0,0:00:29.71,0:00:34.14,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}this is the first time this court has found a state responsible for genocide.
